      en: ["First village in Guyana purchased by freed Africans in November 1839.", "The purchase price was 30,000 guilders, paid entirely in coins.", "The settlement was formerly known as Plantation Northbrook.", "The 83 original buyers came from five neighboring sugar estates.", "Famous for its traditional production of cassava bread and sweets.", "Located approximately 29 kilometers east of the capital, Georgetown."],
