      en: ["Part of the historical Village Movement after 1838.", "Located on the main Corentyne Public Road.", "Situated between Rose Hall and Port Mourant.", "Economically tied to the sugar industry.", "Known for fertile farmland and livestock rearing.", "Houses several Christian churches and schools."],
